genMinDisIdeal -- generalized minimum distance function of an ideal
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        genMinDisIdeal(d,r,I)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

Returns the value of the generalized minimum distance function (GMDF) of the
ideal I on the parameters d and r. The GMDF generalizes the Hamming weights of
Reed-Muller-type codes. The integers d and r indique that the function is
computing the degree of the ideal generated by r-tuples of polynomials of
degree at most d that are linearly independent modulo the ideal I. More
information about the GMDF can be found in Definition 1.1 at
https://arxiv.org/pdf/1812.06529v1.pdf.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : K=ZZ/3;                          |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=K[t1,t2,t3,t4,t5,t6];          |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : I=ideal(t1*t6-t3*t4,t2*t6-t3*t5);|
|                                      |
|o3 : Ideal of R                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : genMinDisIdeal(1,1,I)            |
|                                      |
|o4 = 3                                |
+--------------------------------------+

Ways to use genMinDisIdeal:
===========================

  * "genMinDisIdeal(ZZ,ZZ,Ideal)"

