hyp -- hyp function of an ideal
*******************************

  * Usage: 
        hyp(d,r,I)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

Returns the value of the hyp function (HypF) of the ideal I on the parameters d
and r. The HypF computes the maximum degree of the ideals generated by r-tuples
of polynomials of degree at most d that are linearly independent modulo the
ideal I. Finding upper bounds for this functions is equivalent to finding lower
bounds for the generalized minimum distance function *note genMinDisIdeal:
genMinDisIdeal,. More information about the Hyp can be found in Definition 1.2
at https://arxiv.org/pdf/1812.06529v1.pdf.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : K=ZZ/3;                          |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=K[t1,t2,t3,t4,t5,t6];          |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : I=ideal(t1*t6-t3*t4,t2*t6-t3*t5);|
|                                      |
|o3 : Ideal of R                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : hyp(1,1,I)                       |
|                                      |
|o4 = 1                                |
+--------------------------------------+

