dualCode -- dual of a code
**************************

  * Usage: 
        dualCode(C)
  * Inputs:
      * C, an instance of the type *note LinearCode: LinearCode,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note LinearCode: LinearCode,, 

Description
===========

The dual of a code C of length $n$ over the field $F$ is the code whose
codewords are the elements $v$ in $F^n$ such that for any $c$ in C, the inner
product $<c,v>$ is equal to zero. This function returns the dual of C.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : F=GF(4,Variable=>a);                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C=linearCode(matrix{{1,a,0},{0,1,a}});                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D=dualCode(C)                                            |
|                                                              |
|                                  3                           |
|o3 = LinearCode{AmbientModule => F                           }|
|                BaseField => F                                |
|                cache => CacheTable{}                         |
|                Code => image | a+1 |                         |
|                              | a   |                         |
|                              | 1   |                         |
|                GeneratorMatrix => | a+1 a 1 |                |
|                Generators => {{a + 1, a, 1}}                 |
|                ParityCheckMatrix => | 1 0 a+1 |              |
|                                     | 0 1 a   |              |
|                ParityCheckRows => {{1, 0, a + 1}, {0, 1, a}} |
|                                                              |
|o3 : LinearCode                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

