shorten -- shortens a code
**************************

  * Usage: 
        shorten(LinearCode, List)
        shorten(LindearCode, ZZ)
  * Inputs:
      * C, an instance of the type *note LinearCode: LinearCode,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note LinearCode: LinearCode,, 

Description
===========

Given a code C of length $n$ and a list L (or an integer i), returns a new code
obtained from C by selecting only those codewords of C that have zeros in each
of the coordinate positions in the list L (or the position i), and then
deleting these positions.

The resulting code will have length $n - r$, where $r$ is the number of
elements in L (or 1 when the integer i is used).

