  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note LinearCode: LinearCode,, 

Given a code C of length $n$ and a list L, returns a new code obtained from C
by selecting only those codewords of C that have zeros in each of the
coordinate positions in the list L, and then deleting these positions.

The resulting code will have length $n - r$, where $r$ is the number of
elements in L.

