length(LinearCode) -- returns the length of a linear code
*********************************************************

  * Function: *note length: (Macaulay2Doc)length,
  * Usage: 
        length C
  * Inputs:
      * C, an instance of the type *note LinearCode: LinearCode,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

Given a linear code C over a Galois field, returns the number of entries in any
codeword in C. This parameter is called the length of the code.

This method is provided by the package *note CodingTheory: Top,.

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : C = linearCode(GF(4),{{1,1,1,1}});|
